Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:25:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Checkpoint support: pause before a selected kernel launch

kl_should_checkpoint() picks the launch (KL_CKPT_KERNEL=<name>[:<n>]).
At that launch the hook drains the GPU, creates KL_CKPT_READY and waits
until KL_CKPT_GO exists or it finds itself restored by CRIU (its start
time changes). Also hook hipLaunchKernelExC, hipLaunchCooperativeKernel
and hipExtLaunchKernel, and print kernel names with KL_HOOK_VERBOSE=1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
