+
+## Checkpointing before a kernel
+
+The hook can pause the app right before a chosen kernel launch so that a
+checkpointer (CRIU) can dump it. `kl_should_checkpoint()` in klhook.cc is the
+only place that picks the launch. At that launch the hook drains the GPU
+(`hipDeviceSynchronize`), creates `KL_CKPT_READY` and waits. It continues once
+`KL_CKPT_GO` exists or once it finds itself restored (its start time in
+`/proc/self/stat` changes).
+
+- `export KL_CKPT_KERNEL="vector_square:2"`: checkpoint before the 2nd launch of
+  `vector_square`. The name is the kernel's base name or its mangled name.
+  The launch count defaults to 1.
+- `export KL_CKPT_READY=<file>`: created by the hook when the app is ready to dump.
+  Without it the hook only warns and does not pause.
+- `export KL_CKPT_GO=<file>`: optional. The hook continues once this exists.
+
+`gem5-resources/src/gpu-fs/criu/kl-ckpt.sh` sets all of these and runs CRIU:
+
+```sh
+KL_CKPT_KERNEL=vector_square:2 kl-ckpt.sh [--continue] <ckpt-dir> ./square
+restore.sh <ckpt-dir>
+```
